OpenVDB 13.0 (7c03e1f0) — opt-in flat quad output for VolumeToMesh's uniform
path, upstreamable to AcademySoftwareFoundation/openvdb (extends U10).

Applied to vendor/PicoGKRuntime/openvdb by scripts/fetch-deps.sh. After
changing this patch, re-run scripts/build-deps-wasm.sh (both variants) so the
dependency prefixes reinstall the header.

tools/VolumeToMesh.h — the uniform (non-adaptive) polygon pass allocates two
arrays per leaf (PolygonPool quads + flags) and trims each afterwards; under a
12-thread run those per-leaf allocations serialize on the allocator lock.
enableFlatQuadOutput() routes the same emission (identical per-leaf loop,
identical order, same reverse swizzle) through per-leaf upper-bound slot
ranges of ONE shared array: parallel upper-bound count (the same edge count
the pools were sized with) -> serial prefix sum -> parallel emission recording
exact per-leaf counts. Consumers read flatQuads() +
flatQuadLeafOffsets()/flatQuadLeafCounts(). Off by default; pool path and
adaptive/reference meshing unchanged. Measured on picovoxel SK-0.6 (M2 Pro,
wasm, 12T): polygon phase 3.5 -> 2.1-3.4 ms and allocation-free; the
remaining extraction wall is tree lifecycle (identify/auxdata/clear ~19 of
24 ms), recorded in bench/results/webgpu-v2/sk-0.6-mesh-*.json.

Evidence: bench/results/webgpu-v2/sk-0.6-mesh-*.json.
